      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think instead of world build number the better idea would be just to have something in the quick menu that says \"Last Updated: mm/dd/year\". (although world build number would be useful from a world development perspective on your own world, yeah)\nBut either of the ideas are more preferable to how it is now when we don't know when a map is updated unless you happen to see it on the \"Recently Updated\" playlist.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-02-08T10:30:45.599Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "a long time ago, we could see the world build number in the quick menu. this made it easy to tell if the world actually updated when all you did was update triggers. One day, an update happened that exposed your user ID in the quick menu and streamers freaked out, thinking this was some kind of private info. \nso, you all applied a quick fix to hide that user ID and, you also hid the world build number at the same time, making world development a little more annoying ever since then.\nPlease return the world build number, for your current world, in the quick menu",
